{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkYVNjMwLXAfEynJSHsw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QYGTccLuHvR698pwEwQSvq","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"working":"Start of line, before the first barline: two slash abbreviations. Each one stands for a repeated group of 16ths, so together they are the Eb4 16ths of the first half of the bar. Then a flat note on the Db4 position, stem down, read as a quarter. Then an 8th rest and an 8th note on Db4. That is Db4 quarter, rest 8th, Db4 8th, which is bar 33. Bar 32 would be Db 8th, rest 8th, rest 8th, Db 8th instead. Barline.\n\nNext bar, marked \"rinf.\" and \"pia.\": a half note, read as F4, then a flat half note, Gb4. That is bar 34 (F4 half, Gb4 half).\n\nAfter that, a stretch about two bars long is heavily crossed out. It is dense running 16ths with \"poco for.\" above, ending at a closing barline. It is cancelled, and its music doesn't fit bars 35–36 anyway: those bars hold a G4/Gb3 half, an 8th rest, F3 8ths and a dotted figure, not running 16ths. It looks like a copying slip that was scratched out. Bar 35 presumably starts the next line.\n\nSo the line's readable music is bars 33–34.","right":false,"insights":"What makes this line hard is the long crossed-out stretch. It fills about half the line's width, so a matcher that goes by space or ink density will add phantom bars (here 35–36). The slash abbreviations at the start also hide the 16th pitches. It would be easier to decide if cancelled passages were flagged as deletions and skipped, and bars were counted only from readable notes and barlines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5373,"cache_read_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5373},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"gl